  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "A ceramic substrate carries bottom and top electrodes with the resistor layer between the top electrodes. A primary and a secondary overcoat cover the resistor layer. Each end is wrapped by an edge electrode, a barrier layer and an external electrode."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Derating",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Full rated power holds from -55 °C to 70 °C ambient. Above 70 °C the load falls linearly along curve ②, to zero at 155 °C; curve ② applies to all four sizes, 0805, 1206, 2010 and 2512. Curve ① ends at 125 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Soldering",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The chips suit both reflow and wave soldering and automatic placement."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Environments that degrade the part",
   "page": 12,
   "text": "Liquids of any kind (water, oil, chemicals, organic solvents), outdoor sunlight, dust, salt air and corrosive gases (Cl2, H2S, NH3, SO2, NO2), static or electromagnetic fields, nearby heat sources or flammable materials, resin sealing or coating, and unclean solder or water-based cleaning after soldering can all degrade performance."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Handling",
   "page": 13,
   "text": "Steady loading beyond rated power harms performance and reliability. Tweezers can chip the overcoat or the body. In hand soldering the iron tip must not touch the chip."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Compliance",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "RoHS compliant and halogen free."
  }
